    slug: "content_page_04",
    title_slug: 'term_&_condition',
    title: 'Terms & Conditions',
    description: '<p>Welcome to&nbsp;<strong>Ready Eats</strong>, a digital food delivery platform operated by [Your Company Name]. These Terms and Conditions (“Terms”) govern your engagement as a&nbsp;<strong>Delivery Partner (“Driver”)</strong>&nbsp;with Ready Eats. By signing up or continuing to use our platform, you agree to be bound by these Terms. Please read them carefully.</p><h3>1. Introduction</h3><p>Ready Eats provides an online platform connecting customers with restaurants and independent delivery partners. As a Delivery Partner, you play a key role in ensuring timely, safe, and quality delivery services. These Terms outline your responsibilities, payment policies, conduct guidelines, and the relationship between you and Ready Eats.</p><h3>2. Nature of Engagement</h3><p>You acknowledge that your relationship with Ready Eats is&nbsp;<strong>that of an independent contractor</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>not an employee, agent, or representative</strong>. You retain full control over your working hours, routes, and methods of delivery, subject to customer satisfaction and safety regulations. Nothing in these Terms shall create an employer-employee relationship.</p><h3>3. Eligibility</h3><p>To become a Ready Eats Driver, you must:</p><ul><li>Be at least 18 years old.</li><li>Possess a valid driving license and vehicle registration.</li><li>Hold necessary insurance and comply with all local traffic laws.</li><li>Own a smartphone compatible with the Ready Eats Driver App.</li><li>Pass verification checks including identity, background, and driving record.</li></ul><p>Ready Eats reserves the right to approve, suspend, or terminate access to the platform at its discretion.</p><h3>4. Driver Obligations</h3><p>As a Ready Eats Driver, you agree to:</p><ul><li>Pick up and deliver food orders promptly and safely.</li><li>Handle all orders with care to ensure food quality.</li><li>Follow hygiene, health, and safety guidelines.</li><li>Communicate courteously with customers, restaurants, and support staff.</li><li>Use the Ready Eats app responsibly and maintain active internet connectivity.</li><li>Not engage in fraudulent or unethical behavior.</li></ul><p>Violation of these obligations may result in temporary suspension or permanent termination.</p><h3>5. Payments and Incentives</h3><p>Drivers are compensated for each completed delivery based on distance, delivery time, and service quality. Payment terms include:</p><ul><li><strong>Base Pay:</strong>&nbsp;Fixed delivery fee per order.</li><li><strong>Incentives:</strong>&nbsp;Performance-based bonuses or surge pay during high-demand hours.</li><li><strong>Payment Schedule:</strong>&nbsp;Weekly or bi-weekly transfers to registered bank accounts.</li></ul><p>Ready Eats reserves the right to revise payment structures from time to time, with prior notification.</p><h3>6. Equipment and Expenses</h3><p>Drivers are responsible for providing their own vehicle, fuel, maintenance, and mobile data plan. Ready Eats may provide branded delivery bags or uniforms, which remain company property.</p><h3>7. Ratings and Feedback</h3><p>Customer feedback and ratings determine performance incentives and continued engagement on the platform. Consistently poor ratings may lead to suspension or account review.</p><h3>8. Safety and Compliance</h3><p>Drivers must:</p><ul><li>Follow all traffic laws and local regulations.</li><li>Never operate under the influence of drugs or alcohol.</li><li>Immediately report accidents or safety incidents to Ready Eats Support.</li></ul><h3>9. Account Suspension and Termination</h3><p>Ready Eats may suspend or terminate a Driver’s account for:</p><ul><li>Misconduct or fraud.</li><li>Repeated customer complaints.</li><li>Breach of these Terms.</li><li>Unsafe driving or misuse of company branding.</li></ul><p>Drivers may also voluntarily deactivate their accounts at any time.</p><h3>10. Intellectual Property</h3><p>All logos, trademarks, and digital content on Ready Eats belong to the company. Drivers may not reproduce or misuse any brand assets without authorization.</p><h3>11. Limitation of Liability</h3><p>Ready Eats is not responsible for:</p><ul><li>Vehicle damage, fuel expenses, or personal injury incurred during delivery.</li><li>Losses resulting from technical issues, app downtime, or external factors.</li></ul><h3>12. Dispute Resolution</h3><p>Disputes arising out of these Terms shall first be resolved through internal mediation. If unresolved, they may be referred to arbitration under applicable laws of [Your Jurisdiction].</p><h3>13. Modification of Terms</h3><p>Ready Eats reserves the right to update these Terms periodically. Continued use of the app constitutes acceptance of the latest version.</p>',
    type: 'driver'
